{"id":"u-1830c50d-ff75-486f-86ee-d7b9097c22c0","src":"community","title":"Classic Physique: Phase 1 by Beverly International","author":"Mithosphere","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/EwBJ9u-natural-test-1","desc":"Train 2 days on, 1 day off\n\nDay 1: Legs and Calves - Shoulders\nDay 2: Chest / Triceps\nDay 3: off\nDay 4: Shoulders / Biceps/ Calves\nDay 5: Back\nDay 6: off\n\nA feeder workout is performed two days after your primary workout for a specific bodypart. We have included feeder workouts for the shoulders, lats, and calves – full development of these body parts are essential in developing a classic physique. \n\nThe original standard for a classic physique was that your calves and arms should measure the same. If any single muscle rates as the least developed of all muscles among bodybuilders – it’s the calf. They are stubborn and difficult to develop and require special attention. So don’t neglect your calf work.\n\nDon’t be in a big rush to use as much weight as possible in each exercise. Try to leave each workout knowing you can improve in at least one exercise the next.\n\nThe Hack Squat is preferred if you have the equipment available.\n\nDay 1:\nShoulder Feeder Workout\nShoulder width is key to developing a classic physique, that’s why it is our first “feeder” workout\n\nDay 2:\nFor Bench Press: Dumbbells are preferred if you can give up the barbell bench press in developing squared off “gladiator pecs” preferred in the classic physique. \n\nFor Dumbbell Pullovers:\n“The serratus magnus muscles are the ‘jewel-like’ muscles of your chest … they add width to the chest, shape, muscular definition – as well as classic beauty.” ~ Vince Gironda.\n\nBack Feeder Workout\nShoulder-width Parallel-grip Pulldown (for width) or Under-grip Cable Seated Rows (for back density). \n\nDay4:\nCalf Feeder Workout\nStanding Calf Raise: warm-up x 10-15 reps, 4x25, 1x100 (no weight on the 100-rep set unless you can get the full 100 reps without resting.) Remember what we said earlier about calves. You must bomb them into growth.\n\nDay 5:\nChoose One Feeder Workout, not both:\nSame procedure as back and shoulder feeder workouts.\nChest: Incline Flyes\nQuads: Smith Machine Squats","level":["Intermediate","Advanced"],"goals":["Strength","Muscle"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":90,"joins":0,"rate":0,"rateCount":1,"updated":"2026-08-15T01:34:08.852Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Legs & Calves","Chest, Triceps, & Calves","Conditioning","Shoulder & Biceps","Back","Conditioning"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":12,"pct":50},{"r":10,"pct":60},{"r":8,"pct":70},{"r":6,"pct":75}]},{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":4,"hi":6,"pct":80}]},{"n":"Hack Squat","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":16,"rpe":7,"x":4}]},{"n":"Leg Extension","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Lying Leg Curl","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Stiff Leg Deadlift (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"x":3}]}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Seated Calf Raise","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"x":5}]},{"n":"Calf Raise (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"lo":25,"hi":50,"rpe":10,"x":5}],"note":"No weight"}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":10},{"lo":3,"hi":6,"rpe":10},{"lo":3,"hi":4,"rpe":10}],"note":"One Extended Work set – 6-10 reps (close to maximum), rest for 3-6 deep breaths then 3-6 more reps, 3-4 more breaths then 3-4 reps to failure."}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":12,"pct":50},{"r":10,"pct":60},{"r":8,"pct":70},{"r":6,"pct":75}]},{"n":"Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":4,"hi":6,"pct":80}]},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Chest Fly (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Pullover (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Bench Press (Close Grip)","sets":[{"r":12,"pct":50},{"r":10,"pct":60},{"r":8,"pct":70}]},{"n":"Bench Press (Close Grip)","sets":[{"lo":5,"hi":7,"pct":75}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Tric